§ `ss 83A-33, 83A-45`

#ASSERT `the start-up concession applies` `Chloe's Jarrah shares (c072, d04b)`
#ASSERT NOT `the start-up concession applies` `the same shares at a 20 percent discount`
#ASSERT NOT `the start-up concession applies` `shares in a company incorporated 12 years`

#ASSERT `the ESS discount assessable` `Chloe's Jarrah shares (c072, d04b)` EQUALS 0

§ `s 355-100`

-- d049: turnover under $20 million; the corporate tax rate of 25% is an INPUT (Rates Act s 23, per scenario d04a): 25 + 18.5.
-- 100,000 of notional deductions at 43.5% gives 43,500.
#ASSERT `the R&D offset rate in percent before any premium` 5000000 FALSE 25 EQUALS 43.5
#ASSERT `the R&D offset rate in percent before any premium` 30000000 FALSE 30 EQUALS 30

#ASSERT `the small company's refundable R&D offset` 100000 0 5000000 25 EQUALS 43500

§ `ss 360-20, 360-25`

-- d081: a sophisticated investor (no amount stated; hypothetical). 20% of 500,000 = 100,000; 20% of 1,500,000 capped at
-- 200,000. A retail investor paying more than $50,000 gets nothing; at exactly $50,000, 10,000.
#ASSERT `the early stage investor tax offset` TRUE TRUE 500000 0 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `the early stage investor tax offset` TRUE TRUE 1500000 0 EQUALS 200000
#ASSERT `the early stage investor tax offset` TRUE FALSE 60000 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the early stage investor tax offset` TRUE FALSE 50000 0 EQUALS 10000

